WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.560
- So I hear you love Nashville,

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:02.700
you love stopping in Nashville.

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:04.180
- I'm obsessed with Nashville,

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:06.200
I'm gonna be on Nashville on the tour,

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:09.910
I love going to Nashville
because of the vintage stores,

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:11.990
they have the best vintage shopping.

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:13.440
But I think I might stop doing it 'cause

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:14.620
last time I went, I got this

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:16.580
awesome denim jacket, it had all these,

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:18.490
patches on it and pins and I wore

00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:19.940
it all the time on Instagram like,

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:21.750
I have a horse and you
know, I ride my horse

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:24.510
in this jacket and I loved it so much and

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:26.930
I got this DM one day, from this guy

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:29.787
who was like "Hey, my ex got mad at me

00:00:29.787 --> 00:00:33.240
"and sold a bunch of my
stuff to a vintage store."

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:35.870
(audience gasping and laughing)

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:36.851
I think you have--

00:00:36.851 --> 00:00:38.219
- First of all, that's awesome!

00:00:38.219 --> 00:00:39.467
- I know! (laughing)

00:00:39.467 --> 00:00:41.569
- How have I not thought of that?

00:00:41.569 --> 00:00:43.289
(audience laughing and applauding)

00:00:43.289 --> 00:00:45.240
That is amazing, you're trashing

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:46.807
their stuff plus making profit!

00:00:46.807 --> 00:00:47.920
- Totally!

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:49.630
This woman is an entrepreneur

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:52.080
and she sounds awesome and,

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:53.570
so he said, "Can I have it back?"

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:54.510
and I was like, "Yeah I guess."

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:55.550
so I sent it back to him.

00:00:55.550 --> 00:00:57.410
- Did you tell him, "For
this amount of money"?

00:00:57.410 --> 00:00:58.619
- I know!

00:00:58.619 --> 00:01:02.210
- "Because I bought it, sorry
she's a turd" but, yeah.

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:03.120
- So that, and then the

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:04.570
other thing about going to the south,

00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:06.280
is that I'm still trying
to figure out like, what

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:08.150
everything means and you can probably

00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:09.130
help me with the southern

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:10.660
colloquialisms?
- Ah, yes.

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:12.613
- What does "Bless your heart" mean?

00:01:13.522 --> 00:01:14.355
- Mmm.

00:01:14.355 --> 00:01:16.460
- Does it, it means you're stupid!

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:18.680
- Well, it there's,
- Right?

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:21.260
- There's like, it depends on the tone,

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:22.510
and who you're saying it to.

00:01:22.510 --> 00:01:23.960
- Okay, so when I go to the south,

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:25.327
they'll ask me where
I'm from and I'm like,

00:01:25.327 --> 00:01:26.857
"I live in L.A.", and they're like,

00:01:26.857 --> 00:01:28.572
"Bless your heart."
- "Bless your heart."

00:01:28.572 --> 00:01:30.252
(audience laughing)

00:01:30.252 --> 00:01:31.492
(audience cheering)

00:01:31.492 --> 00:01:32.325
Yep!

00:01:33.550 --> 00:01:35.577
Or it's like, you know
- What does that mean?

00:01:35.577 --> 00:01:37.784
- Its, well it's not a
compliment sometimes.

00:01:37.784 --> 00:01:39.996
(Whitney and audience laughing)

00:01:39.996 --> 00:01:43.423
It's a southerner's
way of, of being shady.

00:01:43.423 --> 00:01:45.130
- Yes! (laughs)

00:01:45.130 --> 00:01:47.150
- But doesn't it sound nice, it's like,

00:01:47.150 --> 00:01:49.311
it's like British people cursing you out.

00:01:49.311 --> 00:01:50.144
- That's so true!
- You know, it's nice!

00:01:50.144 --> 00:01:53.650
It's like, you know it's
rude but I like it, yeah.

00:01:53.650 --> 00:01:56.250
- And then I learned the hard way that

00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:59.337
when a woman, in the south says she's

00:01:59.337 --> 00:02:01.250
"Fixin' to pitch a fit."

00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:02.580
- I'm fixin' to pitch a fit, yeah.

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:04.160
- Get out of there, get out of there.

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:06.350
- Yep, and grab anything that belongs

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:08.240
to you, 'cause she'll sell it too.

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:10.963
(audience laughing)

00:02:10.963 --> 00:02:12.663
A southern woman, no, she's smart.

